## Why This Is Asked
This question tests practical edge deployment, OTA rollout, and telemetry-driven governance for real-world industrial settings.

## Key Concepts
- SageMaker Edge Manager OTA workflow
- Canary and phased rollouts with rollback triggers
- Telemetry-driven monitoring (latency, errors, drift)
- Edge manifest versioning and cryptographic signing
- Cost governance and access control

## Code Example
```json
{
  "EdgeVersion": "v1.2.3",
  "ModelArtifactsS3Key": "s3://bucket/models/maintenance/v1.2.3/model.tar.gz",
  "SignKMSKeyId": "alias/edge-signing-key",
  "RolloutPlan": {
    "CanaryGroup": {
      "DeviceCount": 100,
      "MonitoringDuration": "24h",
      "ApprovalRequired": true
    },
    "Phases": [
      {
        "Name": "Phase1",
        "DevicePercentage": 10,
        "DeviceTypes": ["high-priority"]
      },
      {
        "Name": "Phase2", 
        "DevicePercentage": 30,
        "DeviceTypes": ["critical-infrastructure"]
      },
      {
        "Name": "Phase3",
        "DevicePercentage": 59,
        "DeviceTypes": ["standard"]
      }
    ]
  },
  "RollbackTriggers": {
    "AccuracyThreshold": 0.95,
    "LatencyThresholdMs": 200,
    "ErrorRateThreshold": 0.03,
    "MemoryThresholdPercent": 80
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests multi-tenant inference design, data isolation, cost accounting, and security controls in production ML workloads on AWS.

## Key Concepts
- PrivateLink and API Gateway for private, authenticated access.
- SageMaker Multi-Model Endpoint to share resources.
- Tenant-level quotas and encryption (KMS envelope keys).
- Canary releases, drift monitoring, cost attribution.

## Code Example
```javascript
function route(req){
  const payload = verifyJWT(req.headers.authorization);
  if(!payload.tenant_id) throw new Error('tenant required');
  // quota check…
  return forwardToEndpoint(payload.tenant_id, req.body);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test per-tenant throttling?
- How would you audit data access across tenants?
